posts.body:
Eliaquim said:
I think this script call should work:
Graphics._isFullScreen()
If the game is fullscreen, it will return true.
$gameSwitches.setValue(switchId, Graphics._isFullScreen())
Click to expand...
Hmmm I checked that in console just for fun and it seems to return some kind of object or element or whatever instead of true. I guess the switch checks will still work, but don't know if that can cause some kind of problems that instead of true in the gameSwitches there'll be some kind of long list of stuff.
But yeah, if it matters, you can just write it like:
if (Graphics._isFullScreen()) {
$gameSwitches.setValue(switchId, true);
} else {
$gameSwitches.setValue(switchId, false);
}
